abstract = {<div data-language="eng" data-ev-field="abstract">As part of the 6th Lifelog Search Challenge, this paper presents an approach to arrange Lifelog data in a multi-modal knowledge graph based on cluster hierarchies. We use multiple sequence clustering approaches to address the multi-modal nature of Lifelogs in relation to temporal, spatial, and visual factors. The resulting clusters, along with semantic metadata captions and augmentations based on OpenCLIP, provide for the semantic structure of a graph including all Lifelogs as entries. Textual queries on this hierarchical graph can be expressed to retrieve individual Lifelogs, as well as clusters of Lifelogs.<br/></div> © 2023 Owner/Author.},
